    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d128">

                <pb facs="0360" n="274" sameAs="frus:frus1873p1v1/pg274"/>

                <head>No. 126.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bliss to Mr. Fish</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1872-12-28"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 28, 1872</date>. (Rec’d
                        January 18, 1873.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 440.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I send herewith the text of the decree of
                    the Emperor relieving Prince Bismarck from the presidency of the Prussian
                    ministry, and transferring <pb facs="0361" n="275" xml:id="pg275"/> the duty of
                    the presiding to the “senior minister;” also, the text of the notification of
                    the change to Parliament by Prince Bismarck, stating that Count von Boon will
                    accordingly, from date, assume the presidency.</p>
                <p>I also append an article of the semi-official organ, the “<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Provincial Correspondenz,”</hi> which interprets, it is supposed,
                    authoritatively, the meaning of the change. It must be admitted that the measure
                    is one that, without interpretation, would not explain itself, and that, even
                    thus elucidated, leaves the construction of the Prussian ministry anomalous.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ALEXANDER BLISS.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé
                        d’Affaires</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d128-a1.xml" xpointer="d128-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
